<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργᾰλέος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>painful, troublous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.795
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.667
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄσκρῃ, χεῖμα κακῇ, θέρει
				ἀργαλέῃ</span> (trisyll.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέποτ᾽ ἐσθλῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					640
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					12.11
				</span></i>
			; <i>difficult</i> of attainment, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀληθείη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					114.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάθοδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					43.5
				</span></i>
			:—never in Trag., sts. in Com., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					788
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργαλέας νύκτας ἄγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					764
				</span></i>
			: rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Hier.</u>
					6.4
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.224
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.300
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>troublesome, vexatious,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				1208
			</span></i> codd. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρπ-</span> Bgk.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιότοιο κέλευθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					115.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				450
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				403.5
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				978
			</span></i>: rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὴν ὄψιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					1.61
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργαλέον ἐστί,</span> c. dat. et
				inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δέ μοί ἐστι διασκοπιᾶσθαι ἕκαστον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.252
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				12.410
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				13.312
			</span></i>, etc.: rarely c. acc. et inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργαλέον δέ με πάντ᾽ ἀγορεῦσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.176
				</span></i>
			; or without case, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δὲ πληκτίζεσθ᾽ ἀλόχοισι Διός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.498
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.241
			</span></i>, etc.; also, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			agreeing with the object, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. . . θεὸς
				βροτῷ ἀνδρὶ δαμῆναι</span> God is <i>hard</i> to be
			subdued by mortal man, <i><span class="en">
				4.397
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. γὰρ Ὀλύμπιος ἀντιφέρεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.589
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.499
				</span></i>
			. (By dissimilation from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀλγαλέος,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγος.</span>)</div>
